Local changes to ryanthedev/herdr-md: Linux support (upstream is built and
tested on macOS), and a key help that shows the keys keys.json really binds.

- macOS tools get a Linux counterpart, chosen by window().platform: image size
  from ffprobe (sips), copy through the app clipboard (pbcopy), xdg-open (open,
  open -R, QuickTime Player), the signature helper in place of BSD stat -f.
- Mermaid: the browser is also looked up on PATH (NixOS has none in /usr/bin).
- Help: the "anywhere in Herdr" row lists the keys bound to a pane.split into
  the picker, read from keys(), instead of a fixed cmd-shift-o.

Made against e96cc755eb1afd18209822b638f1e7664685193e; ./herdr-md.nix applies it.
Paths are relative to the upstream repo root (git apply / patch -p1).

